 "notes": "Covered p. 8 from 'PLATE II.' (two rows: line 1 and start of line 2) and all 8 rows of p. 9 (to line 7, ending 'em ren - f / in his name'). No footnotes on p. 8 within the range. Rubric line only over ṭua (p. 8 l. 1). Line numerals inside words: '4.' falls inside nest - k (before V31) and '7.' inside āu (after F40); both words assigned to the line in force at their start (3 and 6). Numeral '3.' stands right before seśep - nef. 'ta ḥer seta - nef' (p. 9 row 7, a name) split into three words at Budge's spaces; numeral 6 falls between ḥer and seta. Square brackets in hieroglyph line only around the χeru signs of maā - χeru on p. 9 l. 6. The small × at every horned viper I9 is part of the I9 type (horns), not a footnote mark; the × before A30 in ṭua is taken as the star N14. Ellipse-shaped D21 used throughout."
